From: Morgan Hough <morgan.hough@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Allow nonempty 0.12 (Fedora 45 dropped 0.10)

t2fanrd only uses NonEmpty::collect/from_vec and iteration, all stable
across 0.10 -> 0.12. Fedora 45 ships nonempty 0.12.0 and no 0.10 compat
crate, so the 0.10 pin makes the package unbuildable there.

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index e5fc99f..f809e90 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ repository = "https://github.com/GnomedDev/T2FanRD"
 [dependencies]
 glob = { version = "0.3.1", default-features = false }
 libc = { version = "0.2.149", default-features = false }
-nonempty = { version = "0.10.0", default-features = false }
+nonempty = { version = ">=0.10, <0.13", default-features = false }
 rust-ini = { version = "0.21.0", default-features = false }
 thiserror = { version = "1.0.50", default-features = false }
 signal-hook = { version = "0.3.17", default-features = false }
